NNAAMMEE
     aauuttoouunnmmoouunnttdd — daemon unmounting automounted filesystems

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     aauuttoouunnmmoouunnttdd [--dd] [--rr _t_i_m_e] [--tt _t_i_m_e] [--vv]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The aauuttoouunnmmoouunnttdd daemon is responsible for unmounting filesystems mounted
     by automountd(8).  On startup, aauuttoouunnmmoouunnttdd retrieves a list of filesys‐
     tems that have the automounted mount option set.  The list is updated ev‐
     ery time a filesystem is mounted or unmounted.  After a specified time
     passes, aauuttoouunnmmoouunnttdd attempts to unmount a filesystem, retrying after
     some time if necessary.

     These options are available:

     --dd  Debug mode: increase verbosity and do not daemonize.

     --rr  Number of seconds to wait before trying to unmount an expired
         filesystem after a previous attempt failed, possibly due to filesys‐
         tem being busy.  The default value is 600, or ten minutes.

     --tt  Number of seconds to wait before trying to unmount a filesystem.  The
         default value is 600, or ten minutes.

     --vv  Increase verbosity.

EEXXIITT SSTTAATTUUSS
     The aauuttoouunnmmoouunnttdd utility exits 0 on success, and >0 if an error occurs.

